      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oil in a large saucepan over medium heat. Fry the shallots and garlic for 2 minutes until softened."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add 1 litre of water and bring to the boil. Add the tamarind paste, fish sauce, and sugar. Stir to dissolve."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the pineapple chunks and tomato wedges. Simmer for 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the fish pieces. Cook gently for 5 to 7 minutes until the fish is just cooked through. Do not stir too much or the fish will break apart."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Taste the broth and adjust with more fish sauce, sugar, or tamarind until the flavour is balanced. It should be sour, slightly sweet, and savoury."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the bean sprouts and stir gently. Remove from heat."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Ladle into bowls. Top with fresh coriander and sliced chilli. Serve with steamed rice."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The fish breaks apart and turns mushy.",
              "cause": "The fish was stirred too much or cooked for too long.",
              "fix": "Add the fish last and cook gently without stirring. As soon as it is opaque all the way through, remove from heat."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The broth is too sour and sharp.",
              "cause": "Too much tamarind was added.",
              "fix": "Add a little more fish sauce and sugar to round out the flavour. A splash of extra water also helps to dilute the sourness."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The bean sprouts are soft and waterlogged.",
              "cause": "They were added too early and overcooked.",
              "fix": "Add the bean sprouts right at the end, just before serving, so they stay crunchy."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Canh chua comes from the Mekong Delta in the deep south of Vietnam. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The river delta is rich in freshwater fish, tropical fruits, and sour vegetables. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each household has its own version, using whatever is in season and local to them. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The soup is always served as part of a larger family meal alongside rice and other dishes. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It is one of the most beloved examples of southern Vietnamese home cooking."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
